    "integrators.scenario2_title": "AI / ML Engine",
    "integrators.scenario2_desc": "Consume measurements, produce health assessments with severity.",
    "integrators.scenario3_title": "CMMS Connector",
    "integrators.scenario3_desc": "Receive work order intents, report completion back.",
    "integrators.scenario4_title": "Historian / Data Lake",
    "integrators.scenario4_desc": "Store all events for time-series analytics and compliance.",
    "integrators.scenario5_title": "Dashboard",
    "integrators.scenario5_desc": "Visualize asset health, trends, and KPIs in real time.",
    "integrators.correlation_title": "Correlation & Traceability",
    "integrators.correlation_subtitle": "One incident, one thread across all systems. Every event in a chain shares the same correlation_id.",
    "integrators.faq_title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
    "integrators.faq1_q": "Do I need to change my PLC firmware?",
    "integrators.faq1_a": "No. IAES lives above the transport layer. Your PLCs keep speaking Modbus, OPC-UA, or whatever protocol they use. IAES standardizes the event format after your gateway or middleware reads the data.",
    "integrators.faq2_q": "What transport does IAES use?",
    "integrators.faq2_a": "Any. IAES is transport-agnostic. Use MQTT for real-time, HTTP for request-response, webhooks for push, or NDJSON files for batch. The standard defines the payload, not the pipe.",
    "integrators.faq3_q": "Is IAES a protocol?",
    "integrators.faq3_a": "No. IAES is a data contract — a JSON schema that defines the shape of industrial asset events. It’s analogous to CloudEvents for cloud-native systems, but designed specifically for industrial equipment.",
    "integrators.faq4_q": "Can I use IAES without Wertek?",
    "integrators.faq4_a": "Yes. IAES is open-source under CC BY 4.0. You can implement it in any system, with any vendor, in any language. Wertek AI maintains the reference implementation, but the standard is vendor-neutral.",
    "integrators.faq5_q": "Do I need to implement all 7 event types?",
    "integrators.faq5_a": "No. Implement only the event types your system produces or consumes. A sensor gateway might only emit asset.measurement. A CMMS connector might only handle work_order_intent and completion.",
    "integrators.cta_install": "Install SDK",
    "integrators.cta_examples": "Browse Examples",
